## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical offline-first data synchronization with versioning, conflict resolution, and tombstones, a common real-world pattern for mobile data apps.

## Key Concepts

- Offline-first sync with local mutation queue
- Versioning and tombstones for deletions
- Conflict resolution strategies (server-wins, client-wins, merge)
- Efficient batching via WorkManager; idempotent retries

## Code Example

```kotlin
@Entity(tableName = "observations")
data class Observation(
  @PrimaryKey val id: String,
  val timestamp: Long,
  val value: Double,
  val version: Long,
  val isDeleted: Boolean = false
)

@Dao
interface ObservationDao {
  @Insert(onConflict = OnConflictStrategy.REPLACE)
  suspend fun upsert(obs: Observation)

  @Query("SELECT * FROM observations WHERE isDeleted = 0")
  suspend fun allActive(): List<Observation>

  @Query("SELECT * FROM observations WHERE timestamp > :since")
  suspend fun recent(since: Long): List<Observation>
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test conflict scenarios end-to-end (offline edits, delayed pushes, concurrent edits)?
- What backend data model and API contract would you define to support delta patches and tombstones safely?

